\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Measured spot radius vs.\ screen displacement, all seven conditions, from the same CSV the growth-slope table above is fit from (\texttt  {ExperimentalComparison/ExP3\_frosted\_screen/measurements/} \texttt  {all\_spot\_measurements.csv}, mtime 2026-09-02). The no-pinhole control's much steeper growth is directly visible, not just implied by the slope ratio in the table; the pinhole conditions' near-overlapping, shallow curves make the non-monotonicity in 600\,$\mu $m's slope (lowest of the six, not the largest or smallest aperture) a real, visually confirmable feature of the raw data rather than a fitting artifact.}}{26}{figure.4.2}\protected@file@percent }
