\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Median worst-case ghost margin vs.\ $N$ (holes requested), all 11 geometry families, every $M$ and the global scope -- the full picture behind the winner table above. Square (cyan) and, separately, golden\_angle (red) are the only families that stay non-negative at $M=0$D and global scope; at every other $M$, square is again the only family that survives with a positive/infinite margin, while most of the remaining 9 families sit well below the $y=0$ safety line regardless of $N$ -- visual confirmation that Model A's structural-safety requirement is a genuinely narrow target, not an easy bar most designs clear. Source: \texttt  {array\_data/evaluation\_results/family\_ranking\_margin\_vs\_N.png}, mtime 2026-09-13 00:37 (pre-generated by this project's own \texttt  {family\_ranking} analysis, not produced for this paper).}}{42}{figure.6.1}\protected@file@percent }
