\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces All three states this section's gate distinguishes, shown side by side for the same two real candidates swept through the identical $(\varphi ,\theta )$ gaze path -- Case A: \texttt  {archimedean\_spiral}, $M=4$D (a real, rejected candidate, $90.79\%$ time-weighted blind); Case B: the shipped hexagonal $M=8$D primary winner ($0.33\%$ blind). Left: Case~A \textbf  {BLIND} ($\varphi =0.2^\circ ,\theta =82.0^\circ $, 0 holes reach the retina). Middle: Case~A \textbf  {GHOST} (5 simultaneously active holes at $\varphi =24.5^\circ ,\theta =243.4^\circ $) -- note the images coincide near $\varphi =0$ but a real ghost-separation only appears at higher $\varphi $, consistent with $\Delta r(s,M)=sM/(P_0-M)$ vanishing only at $M=0$, not at $\varphi =0$. Right: both cases \textbf  {clean}. Frames extracted via \texttt  {ffmpeg} from \texttt  {Array\_Design/array\_geometry\_lab/blindness\_mechanism\_animation/} \texttt  {blindness\_mechanism\_animation.mp4} (mtime 2026-09-16 12:58); the underlying simulation reuses \texttt  {engine/vignetting\_overlap.py}'s validated overlap-area formula and \texttt  {engine/ghost\_formula.py}'s validated separation formula unmodified -- the same two functions used throughout Chapter~\ref {ch:array-theory}.}}{44}{figure.7.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:blindness-states}{{7.1}{44}{All three states this section's gate distinguishes, shown side by side for the same two real candidates swept through the identical $(\varphi ,\theta )$ gaze path -- Case A: \texttt {archimedean\_spiral}, $M=4$D (a real, rejected candidate, $90.79\%$ time-weighted blind); Case B: the shipped hexagonal $M=8$D primary winner ($0.33\%$ blind). Left: Case~A \textbf {BLIND} ($\varphi =0.2^\circ ,\theta =82.0^\circ $, 0 holes reach the retina). Middle: Case~A \textbf {GHOST} (5 simultaneously active holes at $\varphi =24.5^\circ ,\theta =243.4^\circ $) -- note the images coincide near $\varphi =0$ but a real ghost-separation only appears at higher $\varphi $, consistent with $\Delta r(s,M)=sM/(P_0-M)$ vanishing only at $M=0$, not at $\varphi =0$. Right: both cases \textbf {clean}. Frames extracted via \texttt {ffmpeg} from \texttt {Array\_Design/array\_geometry\_lab/blindness\_mechanism\_animation/} \texttt {blindness\_mechanism\_animation.mp4} (mtime 2026-09-16 12:58); the underlying simulation reuses \texttt {engine/vignetting\_overlap.py}'s validated overlap-area formula and \texttt {engine/ghost\_formula.py}'s validated separation formula unmodified -- the same two functions used throughout Chapter~\ref {ch:array-theory}}{figure.7.1}{}}
